QEMU's Windows build accepts clang: -mno-ms-bitfields where the compiler
has no gcc_struct.

mingw-w64 GCC 15 implements __thread with emulated TLS: every access is a
call to __emutls_get_address, and QEMU reads current_cpu, the BQL flag and
RCU state on every device access. Measured 2026-09-17 under wine with a
DOS kernel reading a VGA register in a loop: 52.7 ns a pass on the Linux
build, 121.6 ns on the GCC Windows build, 64.3 ns on a clang one -- the
emulated TLS is most of the Windows penalty on every device access, and a
Glide game polls the Voodoo 2's status register millions of times a
second (Moto Racer at 5 % CPU on a 5900X). clang for x86_64-w64-mingw32
emits native TLS (%gs, _tls_index).

QEMU 9.2 refuses a Windows compiler without __attribute__((gcc_struct)),
which clang does not have. Instead of the error, such a compiler gets
-mno-ms-bitfields -- every struct in the GCC layout, which is what
QEMU_PACKED's gcc_struct asks for -- and QEMU_PACKED drops the attribute
under clang. GCC builds are unchanged. scripts/configure-qemu.sh --windows
builds with clang (packaging/windows/clang-mingw-cc) and --disable-plugins
(lld has no --dynamic-list; nothing here uses TCG plugins).

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -357,7 +357,11 @@
 elif host_os == 'windows'
   if not compiler.compiles('struct x { int y; } __attribute__((gcc_struct));',
                            args: '-Werror')
-    error('Your compiler does not support __attribute__((gcc_struct)) - please use GCC instead of Clang')
+    # 2ksbox: clang (llvm-mingw) has no gcc_struct. -mno-ms-bitfields gives
+    # every struct the GCC layout gcc_struct asks QEMU_PACKED ones for, the
+    # route upstream later took for every Windows build. Clang is what the
+    # Windows package builds QEMU with: mingw GCC has only emulated TLS.
+    qemu_common_flags += '-mno-ms-bitfields'
   endif
 endif
 
diff --git a/include/qemu/compiler.h b/include/qemu/compiler.h
--- a/include/qemu/compiler.h
+++ b/include/qemu/compiler.h
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 #define QEMU_EXTERN_C extern
 #endif
 
-#if defined(_WIN32) && (defined(__x86_64__) || defined(__i386__))
+#if defined(_WIN32) && (defined(__x86_64__) || defined(__i386__)) && !defined(__clang__)
 # define QEMU_PACKED __attribute__((gcc_struct, packed))
 #else
 # define QEMU_PACKED __attribute__((packed))
